# Profile for MiMo-V2.6-Flash-MOPD on two DGX Sparks (GB10), TP=2 EP=2.
# Copy is automatic: ./start.sh writes .env from this file on first run.
#
# Derived from MiaAI-Lab/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-2x-DGX-Sparks (AGPL-3.0) and modified
# 2026-09-28 for the MOPD checkpoint: ModelScope download keys (MS_*), 128
# expert shards, a dual-NIC RoCE channel count, and two memory defaults changed
# after this fleet's own measurements (see "Deviations from upstream" in
# README.md). See LICENSE.
#
# Every value below is either a template placeholder you must edit (the
# cluster / fabric / NFS block) or a measured default for this deployment.
# ~82 GiB of weights per rank out of 121.7 GiB, with the 256 routed experts
# kept in their stored MXFP4 layout.

# ─── cluster ── EDIT THESE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The addresses below are examples from the upstream documentation, not this
# fleet's. Set them to your own fabric addresses (RoCE/QSFP link between the
# two nodes) before the first run.
HEAD_IP=10.0.0.1
WORKER_IPS=10.0.0.2
WORKER_HOSTS=spark2
# Login used for ssh to the worker. Defaults to the same account as the head;
# set it explicitly if the two nodes use different logins.
WORKER_USER=$USER
# The head's ssh identity that is authorised on the worker (passwordless ssh).
SSH_IDENTITY=$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519_shared

# ─── fabric (ConnectX-7) ── EDIT THESE ────────────────────────────────────────
FABRIC_IFACE=enp1s0f1np1
GLOO_SOCKET_IFNAME=enP7s7
NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=enP7s7
IB_HCA=rocep1s0f0,rocep1s0f1
NCCL_NET=IB
NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0
NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=1
NCCL_SHM_DISABLE=1
NCCL_DEBUG=WARN
NCCL_BUFFSIZE=1048576
NCCL_LL128_BUFFSIZE=262144
NCCL_PROTO=^LL128
# 16 = 2 rails x 8 channels. cmd_serve selects every HCA pair that shares a
# subnet between the two nodes (this fleet has two: one per NIC) and merges
# them into a multi-rail NCCL_IB_HCA list; the upstream selector kept only the
# first pair, which is why upstream ships 8. Drop back to 8 if your nodes are
# linked over a single NIC.
NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=16
NCCL_HOST_DIR=$HOME/nccl-2.30.7
NCCL_OVERLAY_PIP=0

# ─── model / image ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The checkpoint lives on the head only; workers read it over NFS.
MODEL_DIR=$HOME/NewModels/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-MOPD
COMMON_MODEL=/var/tmp/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-MOPD
# Authoritative download source. MS_REVISION is the revision this deployment
# downloads and verifies file by file (scripts/verify-weights.py), and the one
# download-ms.sh pins. MS_PYTHON is any interpreter with `modelscope`
# installed; change it to yours.
MS_REPO=XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-MOPD
MS_REVISION=24c7ffbf6a1dd64d8d201b075ff2a19fc68f6bf1
MS_PYTHON=$HOME/ai-stack/venvs/ms/bin/python
# Informational only. HF_REPO/HF_REVISION are never downloaded from here: they
# are reported as the model's `revision` metadata by /v1/models. HF_REVISION
# was read from the HF API and was NOT verified by a download on this fleet.
HF_REPO=XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-MOPD
HF_REVISION=2479e2d0029eca9a34cc7e7f55a121925f81908e
# Gate for the download and for the worker's NFS check. MOPD splits the routed
# experts into 128 shard files (the earlier RL checkpoint had 64).
EXPECTED_SHARDS=128
# Pinned. MiMo-V2.6's MXFP4 experts need sgl-project/sglang#40448 (merged
# 2026-09-20); this is the first nightly that carries it. lmsysorg/sglang:latest
# (v0.5.20, 2026-09-18) and anything older allocate the experts as FP8, ~151 GiB
# per rank, and crash the Spark. serve/doctor rebuild the image when its
# mimo26.base label differs from this value; boot.py refuses a stale engine.
BASE_IMAGE=lmsysorg/sglang:nightly-dev-cu13-20260921-0f6761b5
IMAGE=mimo26-spark:local
HEAD_CTN=mimo26-tp2-head
WORKER_CTN=mimo26-tp2-worker
WORKER_DIR=$HOME/mimo26-tp2
PORT=8888

# ─── weights on the worker ── EDIT THE ADDRESSES ──────────────────────────────
NFS_SHARE=1
NFS_VOLUME=mimo26-tp2-weights
NFS_EXPORT_NAME=mimo26-native
NFS_SERVER_IP_1=10.0.22.1
NFS_CLIENTS=10.0.0.2,10.0.22.0/24,10.0.23.0/24,10.0.33.0/24

# ─── parallelism ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NNODES=2
TP_SIZE=2
EP_SIZE=2
# Cookbook is --dp 2 --enable-dp-attention --mm-enable-dp-encoder next to
# --tp 8. One GPU per Spark, so DP stays 1 and those three flags stay off.
DP_SIZE=1
DIST_PORT=20000

# ─── serving (MiMo-V2.6 SGLang cookbook, tp/ep sized for this fleet) ─────────
# off: weights resident. ssd: HiCache L3 on each node's NVMe (see SSD_DIR).
# ram/cpu is refused — host RAM is GPU memory on Spark.
OFFLOAD_MODE=off
SSD_DIR=$HOME/mimo26-ssd-tp2
WORKER_SSD_DIR=$HOME/mimo26-tp2/ssd
HICACHE_SIZE_GB=4
CONTEXT_LENGTH=1048576
# Budget per rank at TP=2 (boot.py prints the measured line as "preflight:"):
#   experts 75 GiB packed MXFP4 + ~5 GiB sharded attention/dense/embeddings
#   + ~2 GiB encoders ≈ 82 GiB resident (measured 82.92 GB on the head and
#   83.42 GB on the worker for this MOPD checkpoint).
#   SGLang's pool = MemAvailable after the weights (head ~30 GiB, worker ~32)
#   minus 121.7 GiB × (1 - fraction) kept outside for activations. At 0.80 that
#   reserve is 24 GiB and the head has nothing left for the EAGLE draft and
#   KV; 0.85 keeps ~17 GiB outside and leaves ~11 GiB on the head.
# 2026-09-22: 0.85 -> 0.93, deliberately aggressive. The fraction sets what is
# held back as runtime slack, and that slack is pre_model_load_memory x
# (1 - fraction) -- a fraction of the ~112 GB free BEFORE the load, not of
# MemTotal. So 0.85 -> 0.93 takes the slack from 16.80 GB to 7.84 GB and the
# all-pools budget from 10.55 GB to ~19.5 GB.
#
# Measured for this MOPD profile at 0.93: the pool comes back as
# max_total_num_tokens=2546496 with available_gpu_mem=9.15 GB at the end of the
# boot, and the host has 6,186 MiB available. See docs/TEST-RESULTS.md §2.
MEM_FRACTION_STATIC=0.93
HEAD_MEM_FRACTION_STATIC=0.93
# The cookbook runs 128 requests / 16384-token chunks on a 16-GPU node.
# 8 concurrent keeps the prefill transient small on one Spark.
MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS=8
# DEVIATION FROM UPSTREAM: upstream ships 2048 and its Defaults table warns not
# to raise it at mem_fraction_static=0.93. This deployment runs 8192 and has
# booted and served repeatedly with it at 0.93 + MEM_GUARD_GIB=2 (cold-prefill
# ladder in docs/TEST-RESULTS.md §7: 8k-128k rungs, 5/5 OK). The larger chunk
# is what makes 128k prompts 16 chunks instead of 64. Revert to 2048 if your
# boots end with MEMORY GUARD lines in the log.
CHUNKED_PREFILL_SIZE=8192
PAGE_SIZE=64
# KV pin, in full-attention tokens; the SWA pool is derived as
# SWA_FULL_TOKENS_RATIO x this. At ratio 0.03 one pin token costs 7,258 B/rank
# (9 full-attn layers x 2 kv heads x 320 + 0.03 x 39 SWA layers x 4 kv heads
# x 320, fp8), so a full 1,048,576-token context needs 7.09 GiB.
#
# THE PIN IS NOT THE GATE. SGLang clamps it to the budget left after weights
# inside the static fraction. This profile asks for 2,743,808 and the engine
# allocated its profiled value, 2,546,496, logging
# "max_total_tokens=2743808 is larger than the profiled value 2546496".
# Anything at or above 1,048,576 means a single full-context request fits.
MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS=2743808
# Decode CUDA graph capture, tiers 1..N. 8 = MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS, so every
# reachable decode batch replays a graph. This is the big decode lever here:
# EAGLE runs 4 model passes per step (3 draft + verify) over 48 layers, and
# without graphs every one of those launches is eager. 0 disables capture.
CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_BS_DECODE=0
# Prefill-phase graphs. SGLang's own default for prefill is the breakable
# (BCG) backend, so boot.py passes --disable-prefill-cuda-graph unless this is
# 1: prefill capture is untested on this stack and wants the same reserve
# memory as the prefill activation transient. Change one phase at a time.
CUDA_GRAPH_PREFILL=0
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8_e4m3
# The SGLang V2.6 cookbook's Flash recipe value. We ran 0.3 (the V2.5-era
# number) until 2026-09-22, which cost 10x more for the sliding-window pool
# than it needed to: 39 of 48 layers are SWA with 4 KV heads per rank, so one
# SWA token costs 49,920 B/rank against 5,760 B for a full-attention token. At
# 0.3 a full 1M context needs 20.25 GiB of KV; at 0.03 it needs 7.09 GiB, which
# the measured ~7-9 GiB budget can actually cover.
SWA_FULL_TOKENS_RATIO=0.03
# MoE. The experts are packed MXFP4; the runner must consume that layout.
# flashinfer_mxfp4: FlashInfer cutlass MXFP8×MXFP4 on SM120/121, the path this
# fleet runs on its Sparks. marlin (W4A16) is the fallback. auto would fall
# through to the FP8 Triton kernels and fail on the packed tensors. deepep
# (cookbook) needs NVSHMEM across the fabric; none = plain EP.
MOE_RUNNER_BACKEND=flashinfer_mxfp4
MOE_A2A_BACKEND=none
MOE_DENSE_TP_SIZE=1
# Sums expert outputs without the fused atomic-bf16 finalize: byte-identical
# greedy outputs, ~0.3 ms/step.
SGLANG_FLASHINFER_MOE_FUSED_FINALIZE=0
# Release each shard's page cache once its tensors are on the GPU; on
# unified memory that cache is the same pool the KV budget is measured from.
WEIGHT_LOADER_DROP_CACHE=1
# Userspace OOM guard: boot.py kills sglang when MemAvailable drops under
# this many GiB, before the node wedges (the driver path has no OOM killer).
# 0 disables.
# DEVIATION FROM UPSTREAM: upstream ships 4. At MEM_FRACTION_STATIC=0.93 with
# CHUNKED_PREFILL_SIZE=8192 that floor is too high for the FlashInfer autotune
# phase -- the MOPD boot ends near 9.15 GB of available GPU memory and the host
# near 6.2 GiB, so a 4 GiB trigger fires. Measured on this fleet: with
# MEM_GUARD_GIB=4 both ranks were killed during autotune and the only symptom
# was "Server failed to become healthy". 2 leaves air above the trigger and is
# what docs/TEST-RESULTS.md was collected under. Raise it back to 4 if you
# lower MEM_FRACTION_STATIC.
MEM_GUARD_GIB=2
# Cookbook leaves attention on the server default. GB10 uses Triton.
ATTENTION_BACKEND=triton
MM_ATTENTION_BACKEND=triton_attn
# Speculative decoding. The checkpoint ships two drafters; pick one by
# workload. Aggregate tok/s at one stream for this MOPD checkpoint and this
# harness are in docs/TEST-RESULTS.md §8; the per-category median accepted
# length (EAGLE MTP) is the number that explains the split.
#
#   EAGLE   model_mtp.safetensors, 1.2 GiB, 3-layer MTP head. THE DEFAULT.
#           Measured here: median accepted length 2.5-4.0 of 4, best on
#           counting/math (~4.0), lowest on prose (2.50-2.75). Uses
#           SPEC_STEPS / SPEC_TOPK / ENABLE_MTP.
#           Requires CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_BS_DECODE=0 -- decode graph capture
#           crashes under --enable-multi-layer-eagle, it does not merely slow
#           down. Its draft KV pools are ~0.08 GB, so it also buys a much
#           larger KV pool than DFLASH at the same memory fraction.
#   DFLASH  dflash/, a separate 2.9 GiB 5-layer Qwen3 draft model.
#           Not benchmarked in this repository (the EAGLE arm is); upstream
#           reported it ahead on code and behind on prose. Set
#           SPEC_DRAFT_TOKENS=8, CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_BS_DECODE=8 and drop
#           MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS to ~2299968: its drafter keeps a second KV pool
#           sized to the pin (7.94 GB at 1.66M), so the pool is far smaller.
#           Ignores SPEC_STEPS / SPEC_TOPK / ENABLE_MTP. The published
#           dflash/config.json is invalid JSON (trailing comma), so boot.py
#           serves a repaired copy from /state/dflash with the weights
#           symlinked; the checkpoint is never modified.
#   off     no speculation.
SPEC_ALGO=EAGLE
# Verify window, i.e. draft tokens per step. Applies to both algorithms:
# --speculative-num-draft-tokens for EAGLE, and SGLang documents
# --speculative-dflash-block-size as an alias of it for DFLASH.
# 8 is the drafter's own block_size from dflash/config.json (the window it was
# trained for). EAGLE's value was 4. SGLang falls back to the draft config's
# block_size if this is unset, so the two agree.
SPEC_DRAFT_TOKENS=4
# EAGLE only. DFLASH forces both to 1 itself and warns if they differ, so
# boot.py does not emit them under DFLASH.
SPEC_STEPS=3
SPEC_TOPK=1
ENABLE_MTP=1
# DFLASH only; empty means $MODEL_PATH/dflash.
SPEC_DRAFT_MODEL=
REASONING_PARSER=mimo
TOOL_CALL_PARSER=mimo
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=MiMo-v2.6-Flash
# Reporting the bench/ harnesses read. cache-report puts cached_tokens on the
# OpenAI response (it is in the upstream V2.6 recipe); metrics is what makes
# /metrics exist -- without it the endpoint 404s. 0 disables either.
ENABLE_CACHE_REPORT=1
ENABLE_METRICS=1
SKIP_SMOKE=0
SLEEP_ON_IDLE=1
# expandable_segments produced NaN logits on this GB10 stack (README).
PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False
EXTRA_SGLANG_ARGS=
